     "body_en": "The third quarterly report of A-share listed banks has been fully disclosed. A set of data outlines the industry picture and also reflects the challenges faced by stock banks. Statistics show that in the first three quarters of this year, the total revenue of 9 A-share listed stock banks increased by 3.80% and net profit attributable to shareholders down year on year 2.80%, which is the only group with negative net profit growth among all types of listed banks. This means that the joint-stock bank not only lags significantly behind the state-owned banks, but also fails to keep up with the growth of some high-quality urban commercial banks.",
